      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Research in high-stakes professions rarely links cultural communication styles directly to clinical emotional volatility. Instead, observations in these roles often highlight how communication norms impact teamwork; for example, indirect styles might prioritize maintaining interpersonal trust within a unit under stress. Conversely, task-oriented communication valuing directness can sometimes be interpreted—and perhaps criticized—as a lack of emotional empathy or perceived detachment. Ultimately, professional stability in these environments is more strongly correlated with competence, training, and established protocols than with a predicted cultural predisposition toward directness or indirectness.",
